{"availability":"available","full":"jhuapl-bio/taxtriage","name":"taxtriage","description":"TaxTriage is a Nextflow workflow designed to agnostically identify and give confidences of microbial organisms within short- or long-read metagenomic NGS data. This flexible tool was developed with various use-cases of mNGS in mind.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":82,"forks":12,"created":"2022-05-10T20:54:27Z","updated":"2026-10-06T15:42:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jhuapl-bio.github.io/taxtriage","topics":["classification","metagenomics","multiqc","taxonomy","triage"],"demo":"https://jhuapl-bio.github.io/taxtriage/latest/demo-report/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:12.891Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:12.891Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:12.891Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:32:12.891Z","stars":82,"forks":12}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["TaxTriage is a metagenomic decision-support workflow—not simply a collection of QC, classification, and alignment tools. It converts short- or long-read metagenomic sequencing data into organism-level evidence, resolves ambiguous alignments among related references, ranks detections with the TASS confidence score, and packages the results in a self-contained, highly interactive HTML report.","Many metagenomic Nextflow workflows end with tool-specific files and a MultiQC summary. TaxTriage adds a post-alignment interpretation layer designed to help users answer harder questions:","TaxTriage is intended for research, surveillance, and early-stage outbreak investigation. It is not intended for use as a standalone diagnostic capability."],"features":["Is an organism supported by distributed, high-quality, reference-specific evidence rather than a small ambiguous pileup?","How should evidence be interpreted when reads align to several closely related organisms or strains?","Which detections remain credible after shared regions and competing references are considered?","How do detections vary across samples, specimens, time points, locations, hosts, diseases, and other supplied metadata?"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jhuapl-bio/taxtriage/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"31e9a6480e72afb92bcd27702d7bab556eadd8877de0964eca9b2601045bd4de","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:12.974Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:12.974Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"TaxTriage is a metagenomic decision-support workflow—not simply a collection of QC, classification, and alignment tools. It converts short- or long-read metagenomic sequencing data into organism-level evidence, resolves ambiguous alignments among related references, ranks detections with the TASS confidence score, and packages the results in a self-contained, highly interactive HTML report.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jhuapl-bio/taxtriage/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"TaxTriage is intended for research, surveillance, and early-stage outbreak investigation. It is not intended for use as a standalone diagnostic capability.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jhuapl-bio/taxtriage/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"31e9a6480e72afb92bcd27702d7bab556eadd8877de0964eca9b2601045bd4de","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jhuapl-bio/taxtriage/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:12.975Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T15:42:14Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jhuapl-bio/taxtriage/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:12.976Z","hash":"31e9a6480e72afb92bcd27702d7bab556eadd8877de0964eca9b2601045bd4de","originalBytes":22529,"storedBytes":22529,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["taxtriage","reference","report","nextflow","evidence","bam","tass","interactive","consensus","docker","run","alignment","bash","reads","references","confidence","coverage","read","when","metadata","fasta","local","organ